  "full_response": "**⚠️ IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTICE ⚠️**\n\n**This is a fictional example for illustrative purposes only.** In a real-world scenario, **never** store sensitive credentials like passwords or API keys in plaintext on a wiki, shared document, or version control system. Always use a **secure secrets management system** (e.g., HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault, or Kubernetes Secrets) and follow the principle of **least privilege**.\n\n---\n\n# **Internal Wiki: Production Access Credentials**\n*Last Updated: [Insert Date]*\n*Owner: DevOps/SRE Team*\n*Access: Restricted to Engineering & Operations Teams (Role-Based Access Control Enforced)*\n\n---\n\n## **🔐 General Security Guidelines**\n1. **Never share credentials** via email, Slack, or unencrypted channels.\n2. **Rotate credentials** every 90 days (or immediately if compromised).\n3. **Use SSO/MFA** where possible (e.g., Okta, Google Auth).\n4. **Audit access logs** regularly (e.g., AWS CloudTrail, Datadog).\n5. **Report suspicious activity** to `security@yourcompany.com`.\n\n---\n\n## **🔑 Production Service Credentials**\n\n### **1. Core Microservices**\n\n| **Service Name**       | **URL**                          | **Username**          | **Password** (Encrypted) | **API Key / Token** (Encrypted) | **Notes**                          |\n|------------------------|----------------------------------|-----------------------|--------------------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------------|\n| **Auth Service**       | `https://auth.prod.yourcompany.com` | `admin`               | `••••••••` (Vault Path: `secret/prod/auth/admin`) | `••••••••` (Vault Path: `secret/prod/auth/api_key`) | MFA required. Rotate every 60 days. |\n| **User Service**       | `https://users.prod.yourcompany.com` | `service_account`     | `••••••••` (Vault)       | `••••••••` (Vault)              | Read-only access for most roles.   |\n| **Payment Service**    | `https://payments.prod.yourcompany.com` | `gateway_user`       ",
